---
import Base from '../layouts/Base.astro';
---

<Base
  title="About — Emmanuel Utulu"
  description="Emmanuel Utulu is a software engineer in Lagos, Nigeria, who designs. Background in software engineering, practice in brand and poster design."
>
  <section class="page pt-14 md:pt-20">
    <p class="meta">About</p>
    <h1 class="display-line mt-6 max-w-[20ch]">I build the thing, then I make it make sense.</h1>
  </section>

  <section class="page mt-14 grid gap-12 md:mt-20 md:grid-cols-[1fr_1.15fr] md:gap-20">
    <div>
      <div
        class="relative aspect-[4/5] w-full max-w-sm overflow-hidden border border-[var(--color-green-deep)] bg-[var(--color-green-deep)] text-[var(--color-paper)]"
      >
        <div class="flex h-full flex-col justify-between p-5">
          <span class="font-mono text-[0.6875rem] uppercase tracking-[0.06em] text-[var(--color-green-lift)]">
            U2LU
          </span>
          <span class="font-display leading-[0.78] tracking-tight" style="font-size: clamp(4.5rem, 11vw, 7.5rem);">
            EU
          </span>
          <span class="font-mono text-[0.6875rem] uppercase tracking-[0.06em] text-[var(--color-green-lift)]">
            Lagos · Nigeria
          </span>
        </div>
      </div>
      <dl class="mt-8 space-y-4 text-sm">
        <div class="flex justify-between gap-6 border-t border-[var(--color-rule-soft)] pt-3">
          <dt class="meta">Based</dt>
          <dd>Lagos, Nigeria (WAT)</dd>
        </div>
        <div class="flex justify-between gap-6 border-t border-[var(--color-rule-soft)] pt-3">
          <dt class="meta">Focus</dt>
          <dd class="text-right">Front-end engineering, interface design</dd>
        </div>
        <div class="flex justify-between gap-6 border-t border-[var(--color-rule-soft)] pt-3">
          <dt class="meta whitespace-nowrap">Open to</dt>
          <dd class="text-right">Full-time roles, occasional design work</dd>
        </div>
      </dl>
    </div>

    <div class="max-w-[60ch] space-y-5 text-[var(--color-fg-soft)]">
      <p class="text-lg text-[var(--color-fg)]">
        I studied software engineering because I liked it — not because it was the safe option.
      </p>
      <p>
        Design arrived sideways. Someone needed a YouTube thumbnail, I said yes, and that one
        favour turned into posters, event identities and campaign work. I got faster at it because
        I enjoyed it, and because a client was waiting.
      </p>
      <p>
        The two things don’t compete. Design taught me to decide what a page should say before
        adding anything to it. Engineering taught me that a beautiful decision is worthless if it
        ships broken, slow, or unnavigable on a phone.
      </p>
      <p>
        Right now I’m working towards the same thing from both sides: applications that are
        finished, deployed, and worth using. React and TypeScript on the front, learning the rest
        of the stack properly rather than skimming it.
      </p>
      <p>
        When I’m not building, I’m usually looking at type, football, or both.
      </p>
      <div class="flex flex-wrap gap-3 pt-2">
        <a class="btn btn-ghost" href="mailto:ayoutulu@gmail.com">Email me</a>
        <a
          class="btn btn-ghost"
          href="https://www.linkedin.com/in/emmanuel-utulu/"
          rel="noopener"
          target="_blank">LinkedIn ↗</a
        >
      </div>
      <p class="meta pt-2">CV — being updated. Ask me for the current version.</p>
    </div>
  </section>
</Base>
